Students are expected to know and understand the characteristics and context of the whole play
they have studied.

One extract from each set play is printed in the question paper. Students answer questions relating
to that extract, referring to the whole play as appropriate to the demands of the question.

Where relevant they may support their answers with sketches or diagrams.

All students must be prepared to answer questions from the perspective of a performer.

The exam will include one compulsory short answer question for all students linking design and
context and/or theatrical conventions. Students don't need to have gained practical experience of
design to answer this question.

One part of Section B will offer students the choice of answering as either a performer or designer
(lighting, sound, set, costume, puppets).

