C:\Users\tshau\Documents\Study Vault\scripts\_retrofc\units\drama-aqa__around-the-world-80-days\raw\L01.txt:12: <p data-narration-id="n2">Jules Verne published his adventure novel in 1872, at a moment when two technologies had just made circumnavigation in eighty days theoretically possible: the Suez Canal opened in 1869 and the American transcontinental railroad was completed in the same year. Verne imagined a precise English gentleman betting £20,000 at his gentlemen's club that he could complete the journey &mdash; and the result is a breathless chase spanning India, Hong Kong, Japan, San Francisco and the Atlantic. Laura Eason's 2013 stage adaptation, which premiered at the New Vic Theatre in Newcastle-under-Lyme in a theatre-in-the-round configuration, distils this chase into something even tighter: eight actors playing every role in the story, from Phileas Fogg himself to train conductors, customs officials, ship&rsquo;s captains and a herd of elephants. Understanding the <dfn class="term" data-def="A play built from a series of short, self-contained scenes rather than a continuous unfolding action.">episodic structure</dfn> of this adaptation is the starting point for all the staging and performance work that follows.</p>
C:\Users\tshau\Documents\Study Vault\scripts\_retrofc\units\drama-aqa__around-the-world-80-days\raw\L01.txt:14: <div class="key-fact" data-narration-id="n3" data-revision-tip="Cover this and recall: where and when did Eason's stage adaptation of Around the World in 80 Days premiere, and in what theatre configuration?">
C:\Users\tshau\Documents\Study Vault\scripts\_retrofc\units\drama-aqa__around-the-world-80-days\raw\L01.txt:16: <p>Eason&rsquo;s adaptation premiered at the New Vic Theatre, Newcastle-under-Lyme in 2013, directed by Theresa Heskins, in a theatre-in-the-round configuration with a cast of eight actors multi-roling throughout.</p>
C:\Users\tshau\Documents\Study Vault\scripts\_retrofc\units\drama-aqa__around-the-world-80-days\raw\L01.txt:70: "text": "Identify the staging configuration used in the world premiere of Around the World in 80 Days at the New Vic Theatre in 2013.",
